  "content": {
    "title": "Atletico overcomes Barcelona in Champions League thriller: Recap, highlights",
    "text": "Updated April 14, 2026, 5:10 p.m. ETAtlético Madrid is heading to the UEFA Champions League semifinal after overcoming La Liga rival Barcelona in a thrilling quarterfinal.Barcelona defeated Atlético 2-1 in the second leg on Tuesday, April 14, but the capital club advanced with a 3-2 aggregate victory after last week's win in Barcelona.The visitors managed to level the tie within the first 24 minutes as Lamine Yamal and Ferran Torres scored quickly at the Metropolitano Stadium.But Ademola Lookman scored in the 31st minute to put Atlético back in front on aggregate, with the Nigerian's goal standing up for the next hour of play.Like it did in the first leg, Barcelona finished the game with 10 men after Eric García was shown a straight red late in the contest.FINAL: Atletico Madrid 1-2 Barcelona (3-2 agg.)That's it! Atletico Madrid is heading for the semifinal after a thrilling second leg. 90+6' - Atletico Madrid 1-2 BarcelonaAraujo heads over! That was the chance for the Uruguayan, who had a great look from close range. 80' - Barcelona red card! Eric GarciaJust like the first leg, Barcelona has a defender sent off for denying an obvious scoring chance! This time it's Garcia who brings down Sørloth from behind. The play is initially ruled offside but after a VAR check, the Norway forward is ruled onside and Garcia is off. 73' - Atletico Madrid 1-2 BarcelonaHuge save by Garcia! The Barcelona goalkeeper makes himself big and denies Le Normand from close range. That could have been tie over. 55' - Ferran Torres goal disallowed!It looks like Torres leveled the tie on aggregate for the second time tonight, but it's waved off due to offside! Gavi's shot is blocked by Lenglet but the ball loops up to Torres, who volleys home.After a brief check, it's waved off. 46' - Atletico Madrid 1-2 BarcelonaWe are underway in the second half. HALFTIME: Atletico Madrid 1-2 BarcelonaThat concludes a wild first half, with Atletico ahead 3-2 on aggregate after Lookman replied to goals from Yamal and Torres. Ademola Lookman goal! Atletico goes back in frontAtletico Madrid's Ademola Lookman scored in the 31st minute to put his team back in front on aggregate after Barcelona had erased its two-goal deficit within the first time 25 minutes. Ferran Torres goal! 2-2 on aggregateBarcelona's two-goal comeback didn't take long to complete with Ferran Torres scoring in the 24th minute to make it 2-2 on aggregate in this Champions League quarterfinal. Lamine Yamal goal!Barcelona halved Atletico's 2-0 advantage from the first leg just four minutes in with Lamine Yamal scoring a goal to make it 2-1 on aggregate. KickoffWe are underway! Lamine Yamal channels LeBron JamesBarcelona star Lamine Yamal changed his Instagram profile picture to LeBron James before the match.The Barcelona star didn't just use any image of James, but a picture of him holding the championship trophy after the 2016 NBA Finals.Yamal said he's hoping Barcelona can emulate the Cleveland Cavaliers in that series, producing an epic comeback. Atletico Madrid lineup vs. Barcelona Barcelona lineup vs. Atletico MadridHow to watch Atletico Madrid vs BarcelonaWhen: Tuesday, April 14Where: Metropolitano Stadium (Madrid, Spain)Time: 3 p.m. ETChannel/streaming: Paramount+ (WATCH HERE), ViX (Watch on Prime Video), Univision, TUDNAtletico Madrid vs. Barcelona game oddsAtletico Madrid vs. Barcelona prediction, pickIf any team in the world has the firepower to overcome a two-goal deficit away from home, it's Barcelona. However, Simeone's vast experience in these situations should be enough to see out the tie in the end.Prediction: Atletico Madrid 2, Barcelona 2",
